text In the afternoon, we do work in the attic.
text After running tests with a multimeter, I notice that not much current is going to the outlets on the second floor. It seems likely that there's a short circuit somewhere.
text Still, the distribution board has a short circuit prevention switch, so it seems extremely unlikely that a fire or something else would break out.
text But we were called out because her circuit breaker would frequently trip, so that's what we need to fix.
sound MSI.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text What does the multimeter say?
text @[Tomoya]
text It's not moving.
sound MSJ.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text Then I'll go a little farther in. When I give you the signal, flip the breaker and test the circuit.
text @[Tomoya]
text Got it.
text Yoshino-san disappears inside.
text I look into the attic after him, and then I see Yoshino-san flick his flashlight off and on twice.
text That's the signal.
text I check the current; the resistance that was there before is gone now.
text @[Tomoya]
text Looks okay.
sound MSK.aac
text @[Yoshino]
text All right, bring me thirty centimeters of cable. Peel both sides back by four centimeters.
text I make the wire according to his specifications and hand it to him.
